# ZL Splitter for WebCLAP

ZLSplitter by ZL Audio (zsliu98), a splitter that splits audio into left/right, mid/side, low/high,
transient/steady or peak/steady, ported to WebCLAP. This is not an official ZL Audio release.

- ZLSplitter: https://github.com/ZL-Audio/ZLSplitter (commit a8f31f6, after version 0.3.0)
- This port, and the complete source of this bundle: @SOURCE_URL@
  Build it with `scripts/build-zl-splitter.sh`, which fetches every dependency below at the commit named here.

Changes in this port (`patches/zl-splitter-webclap.patch`): the editor's analyzer loop, which runs on a thread
upstream, runs one pass per repaint on the editor's thread, and the processor builds without its editor.
Upstream has two stereo outputs, one per part. The bundle has one stereo output, which carries output 1 (left,
mid, low, transient or peak); the Swap parameter puts the other part there. The editor has no colour settings,
no import or export of control settings, no tooltip language setting (tooltips are in English) and no Credit tab:
the UI settings panel shows a one-line legal notice instead, and the credits are below. UI settings the editor
saves live in the page's memory and are gone when it reloads.

